## Environment for the dbt multi-catalog demo.
##
##   cp .env.example .env
##   set -a && source .env && set +a     # (or `direnv allow` if you use direnv)
##   dbt seed && dbt run
##
## Source this from the repo root (the `${PWD}` defaults below assume that).
## With direnv, `.envrc` loads `.env` and derives DBT_PROFILES_DIR / DUCKDB_HOME
## when they are absent, and it also sources an optional git-ignored
## `.envrc.private` — put the credential sections below in a file outside the
## repo and source it from there instead of copying secrets into `.env`.
## The default catalog (ducklake) needs NO credentials, and the published dbt
## Fusion CLI needs no custom build (see README → "Install dbt").
## Lines that are commented out are OPTIONAL: only needed for the external
## catalog named in their section, and only when you also uncomment that
## catalog's block in catalogs.yml + profiles.yml.

## ──────────── derived — leave as-is ────────────
## Where dbt finds profiles.yml / catalogs.yml (this repo):
DBT_PROFILES_DIR=${PWD}
DUCKDB_HOME=${PWD}/.tmp/duckdb-home

## ──────────── OPTIONAL — catalog: horizon (Snowflake) ────────────
## External-engine WRITES to Horizon need KEY-PAIR auth (a PAT can read but not
## write — createTable 403s). One-time: scripts/configure_horizon_schema.sh.
## Each session: scripts/refresh_horizon_token.sh mints HORIZON_ACCESS_TOKEN from
## the SNOWFLAKE_* key-pair (~55 min). Then uncomment the horizon block in
## catalogs.yml + the snowflake_oauth secret in profiles.yml.
# SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT=
# SNOWFLAKE_SQL_API_HOST=${SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT}.snowflakecomputing.com
# SNOWFLAKE_USER=
# SNOWFLAKE_ROLE=
# SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE=
# SNOWFLAKE_PRIVATE_KEY=                 ## base64 DER or PEM; signs the Horizon JWT
# HORIZON_ENDPOINT=https://${SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT}.snowflakecomputing.com/polaris/api/catalog
# HORIZON_OAUTH2_SERVER_URI=${HORIZON_ENDPOINT}/v1/oauth/tokens
# HORIZON_OAUTH2_SCOPE=session:role:YOUR_ROLE
# HORIZON_WAREHOUSE=                     ## the Horizon catalog (database) name
# HORIZON_SCHEMA=AWS_CLOUD_COST          ## UPPERCASE — REST namespace is case-sensitive on write
# CATALOG_SCHEMA=AWS_CLOUD_COST          ## makes generate_schema_name emit the uppercase namespace
# HORIZON_ACCESS_TOKEN=                  ## written by scripts/refresh_horizon_token.sh (do not hand-edit)
# SNOWFLAKE_EXTERNAL_VOLUME=FUSION_ADAPTERS_CI_TEMP  ## a real S3 volume w/ ALLOW_WRITES=TRUE (not SNOWFLAKE_MANAGED)
# SNOWFLAKE_BASE_LOCATION_ROOT=dbt_aws_cloud_cost/horizon
# SNOWFLAKE_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1     ## must match the external volume's region

## ──────────── OPTIONAL — catalog: mdls (Iceberg REST — Polaris) ────────────
# POLARIS_URL=
# POLARIS_ID=
# POLARIS_SECRET=
# POLARIS_WAREHOUSE=aws_cloud_cost
# POLARIS_OAUTH_TOKEN_URI=${POLARIS_URL}/v1/oauth/tokens
# POLARIS_OAUTH_SCOPE=PRINCIPAL_ROLE:ALL
# POLARIS_ACCESS_DELEGATION_MODE=VENDED_CREDENTIALS
# POLARIS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1

## ──────────── OPTIONAL — target: dbt_compute (Alt engine, Fivetran-managed) ────────────
## Queries an MDLS destination through the staging dbt-compute service instead
## of DuckDB. Selected via `x_alt_target: dbt_compute` in profiles.yml.
## DBT_COMPUTE_AUTH_TOKEN is a JWT minted with quack's dbt-compute-gen-token
## (crates/dbt-compute/README.md) for a --group-id that must already be
## registered in the staging deployment's MDLS_CONFIGS — ask whoever manages
## that deployment to add your group before this will resolve. Needs a
## fs-built `dbt` (the published CLI doesn't support `type: alt` yet) plus the
## adbc_driver_dbt built via quack/scripts/build-adbc-driver-local.sh.
# DBT_COMPUTE_AUTH_TOKEN=
# DBT_COMPUTE_ORG=fivetran
# DBT_COMPUTE_DATABASE=                 ## the Fivetran group/destination id
# DBT_COMPUTE_SCHEMA=                   ## must already exist/be authorized — new namespace creation is denied

## ──────────── OPTIONAL — catalog: unity (Databricks; read-write) ────────────
# DATABRICKS_HOST=https://<workspace>.cloud.databricks.com
# DATABRICKS_TOKEN=
# DATABRICKS_CATALOG=main
# DATABRICKS_SCHEMA=aws_cloud_cost
# DATABRICKS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-west-2

## ──────────── OPTIONAL — catalog: r2 (Cloudflare R2 Data Catalog) ────────────
## Enable R2 in the Cloudflare dashboard, create a bucket, then:
##   wrangler r2 bucket create <bucket>
##   wrangler r2 bucket catalog enable <bucket>   # prints Catalog URI + Warehouse
## Mint an Account R2 API token with "Admin Read & Write" (covers R2 Data Catalog
## + storage) for R2_TOKEN_VALUE. Writes work on stock DuckDB — no #1017 needed.
# R2_CATALOG_URI=https://catalog.cloudflarestorage.com/<account_id>/<bucket>
# R2_WAREHOUSE=<account_id>_<bucket>
# R2_TOKEN_VALUE=

## ──────────── OPTIONAL — catalog: s3_tables (Amazon S3 Tables) ────────────
## AWS auth uses the standard credential chain (configure AWS SSO/profile).
# AWS_REGION=us-west-2
# AWS_S3_TABLES_WAREHOUSE=arn:aws:s3tables:<region>:<account>:bucket/<bucket>
# AWS_S3_TABLES_NAMESPACE=cloud_cost
